      "intent": {
        "task": "Reduce all four source fractions while tracking scalar factors and original real domains.",
        "source_solution": "I cancels y-10 to y^2+10y+100 with y!=10. II has denominator 3(2x+3), giving (4x^2-6x+9)/3 with x!=-3/2. III has a^3-216=(a-6)(a^2+6a+36), with a^2+6a+36=(a+3)^2+27>0; canceling that quadratic gives 1/(a-6), a!=6. IV cancels 9b^2+12b+16 from numerator 2 times that factor, giving 2/(3b-4), b!=4/3.",
        "unit_reason": "A complete result/domain list unifies cancellation, remaining scalar factors, and removable exclusions without turning four denominators into independent clicks. Row III now offers different first-factor orientations and signs to judge. D has the same correct I, II and IV rows as C and differs only in III, so those other rows cannot eliminate it. Whole-list selection still does not certify independently produced working or separate mastery of every row.",
        "concept_blocks": [7, 10],
        "limitations": ["A correct complete list does not establish independently produced factor-and-cancel steps."],
