          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "I, II and IV now match the correct complete option, including original domains. Only III is false: it requires first factor a-6, not a+6. At a=0 the original is -1/6 but the candidate is 1/6; the candidate also introduces an invalid pole at a=-6.", "misconception": "For III, falsely write a^3-216=(a+6)(a^2+6a+36), mixing a sum first factor with the difference quadratic, then cancel the quadratic to obtain 1/(a+6) while retaining the original exclusion a!=6."}
